 "summary": "The 5-day version of nSuns 5/3/1 LP, adding a heavy overhead-press day with incline bench to the 4-day layout. Every day pairs a 9-set main lift with an 8-set secondary lift, and training maxes rise weekly from the heavy-single AMRAP.",
 "evidenceNote": "Very high volume: 17 sets of main lifts per session, with pressing on three days a week (flat bench Monday and Friday, incline Wednesday; 34 bench, incline and close-grip sets a week on the 5-day version). Most sets sit well short of failure while the 1+ and final '+' sets are near-maximal. It suits intermediates coming off a novice program who can recover from long sessions. Known weaknesses: sessions are long, TM jumps based on one single can outrun real strength and lead to stalls, and accessory work is left entirely to the lifter.",
 "sources": [
  {
