   "kind": "article"
  }
 ],
 "schedule": "5 days a week per the spreadsheet: Monday volume bench + OHP, Tuesday squat + sumo deadlift, Wednesday OHP + incline bench, Thursday deadlift + front squat, Friday heavy bench + close-grip bench.",
 "progression": {
  "type": "PERCENT_TM",
  "description": "Training max (TM) starts at 90% of your 1RM (spreadsheet: CEILING(1RM*0.9)). Each week, the '1+' set (95% x1+) on a lift's T1 day sets that lift's TM change for the next week (squat: Tuesday; OHP: Wednesday; deadlift: Thursday; bench: Friday - Monday's volume bench has no 1+ set, only a final 8+ set). Spreadsheet rule (lb): 0-1 reps no increase; 2-3 reps +5 lb; 4-5 reps +5-10 lb; more than 5 reps +10-15 lb. Approximate kg conversion (not in the source; the sheet rounds kg loads to 2.5 kg): 0-1 reps +0; 2-3 reps +2.5 kg; 4-5 reps +2.5-5 kg; 6+ reps +5-7.5 kg. The spreadsheet also says to raise the TM each week if all reps were completed, and that the new TM is entered manually. T2 lifts use percentages of the related main lift's TM (OHP from OHP, sumo deadlift from deadlift, incline and close-grip bench from bench, front squat from squat).",
  "incrementKg": {
   "upper": 2.5,
   "lower": 2.5
  },
  "deload": "No scheduled deload in the author's spreadsheet. A 0-1 rep result on the 1+ set means no TM increase that week; no further reset rule is given in the official sheet."
 },
